Version 5 (V5)

I’ve added the converter, a time calculator and a 12/24hour chart to Minimal 24 Clock, with a side menu to reach them. 
This is version 3.0 as Minimal24Clock_v5.apk. It’s signed with the same key as before, so it installs over your current 
version and keeps your widget and settings. I tested the time reading and conversion on a computer, but I haven’t run the screens on a phone.

Side menu (☰)

🕒 Clock layout: the live preview, time layout, date, alignment and size.
🔤 Font: builtin fonts, your own font files, and the style.
🎨 Colour & shadow: light/dark mode, text colours and shadow.
🔁 12 ⇄ 24 converter
➕ Time calculator
📊 12 / 24 chart
ℹ About: your details now show “Coimbatore, Tamil Nadu, India”.

Converter

Type a time in either style, for example 3:45 PM, 3.45 p.m., 15:45, 1545 or 9 pm.
It converts to the other style and says which one the answer is in. For example, it tells you “15:45 is 24hour time” and 
shows the 12hour time too. It also writes the time in words, such as “three fortyfive in the afternoon”.
“I’m typing” has three choices: Autodetect, 12hour or 24hour. If you type something like 3:45 with no AM or PM, Autodetect 
can’t tell which style you mean. It then shows both answers instead of guessing.
Buttons: Now fills in the current time, Copy result copies the answer, and Clear empties the box.
Bad input gets a plain message, such as “Minutes must be between 00 and 59”.

Time calculator

Add / subtract: for example, 9:30 PM plus 2 hours 45 minutes. The answer is shown in both styles and says whether it lands 
on the same day, the next day or the previous day. There are quick buttons for 15 min, 30 min, 1 hour and so on.
Difference: the time between two times, such as 9:30 AM to 5:15 PM, which also works across midnight.
Add AM or PM for 12hour time. Without it, the time is read as 24hour.

Chart

It shows the current time live in both styles, with short rules for converting each way.
The chart lists every hour, every 30 minutes or every 15 minutes in the 24hour, 12hour and timeofday columns. The row for the 
current time is highlighted and the PM rows are lightly shaded. Tap any row to open it in the converter.

